Z||000016||DRH||06-05-2001||11:03 PM||||I grew up in Alabama and the generic reference to soft drinks was usually 'coke'. The REAL rednecks out in the country might call it a 'cold drink'. 'Soda' or 'Pop' either one would get you a "Y'all ain't from 'round these parts, are ya" look. That seemed to hold true most places I lived in the south (TN, KY, GA). <P>Northeast PA seemed like a lot of people called it 'soda'.<P>Here in western WI it's seems like everybody calls it 'pop'. <P>||||reg||1
