Z||000026||Ditz88GT||06-06-2001||09:40 AM||||Soda||||reg||7
Z||000027||stsmithgt||06-06-2001||10:04 AM||||Saying "soda", is short for "carbinated drink" around here.  You ask someone if they want a soda if you have a variety and if they say yes, you say, "what kind?  We have....".  Or if there are only Pepsi in the frig., you would ask if they want a pepsi. Simple and literal. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>"Drinks" found around the shop:<BR>Coke=140 cal.<BR>Coke obviously says cola on the can.(Cocacola)<BR>V8=70 cal.<BR>Diet Pepsi=0 cal.<BR>PepsiOne=1 cal.<BR>Pepsi says cola on the can.<BR>Vintage lemon-lime soda=160 cal.&lt;-cheap soda<BR>(it says SODA on the can, not pop or cola) someone gave it to me at work about six months ago and I still haven't drank it. he he||||reg||1
Z||000028||Carrolles||06-06-2001||10:17 AM||||When I grew up in New Orleans everything was either called "Coke" or "Soft Drink".<P>I've lived in Houston, TX for 13 years and I now live in Birmingham, AL.  It's still "Coke" or "Soft drink" or the actual name by brand (Pepsi, DP, Coke, or whatever I have on hand at the time).||||reg||1
Z||000029||87GTBro||06-06-2001||11:51 AM||||I have to agree with all the Texas folk.  I live at the bottom of the world.  We call it a "coke" or we refer to each "coke" by their proper names... (i.e. DP, Pepsi, Coca Cola, Sprite)<P>I have a friend from North Dakota who calls them "pop"  I always make fun of him when I hear him say it.  There's nothing wrong with it.  It's just the way he was raised.  Up north, they call it "pop".  Down here, we call it "coke" or "soda".<P>It's kinda like in Canada, the kids are taught in school that the last letter of the alphabet is "Zed" and in the U.S., we were taught that it is plain old "Z".<P>It all depends on how you grew up...  but "pop" still sounds funny!!!!!  If someone asks me if I want a "pop" I am more than likely going to defend myself!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000030||coolcat||06-06-2001||11:59 AM||||in my neck of the woods coke = soda no matter what u want u ask for a coke.<P>------------------<BR>Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||1
Z||000031||stsmithgt||06-06-2001||12:05 PM||||Sounds like the coke comercials work the best. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000032||fierojunky||06-06-2001||12:13 PM||||just pop here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000033||Denny||06-06-2001||12:56 PM||||I do believe "pop" is mostly an "Appalachian chain" term . . . I grew up in Johnstown, PA, and all my life it was "pop." Moved to Lancaster Co. and suddenly it was "soda." People looked at me like I had 2 heads when I said "pop," so . . . . ||||reg||6
Z||000034||starfighter007@msn.com||06-06-2001||06:12 PM||||I'm from chicago lived there for 30 of my 42 years now live here in phx.az.I've always called it by its correct name witch is pop now my wife who was born and raised here by the way who is a big dork calls it soda how ridiculios especially when everybody knows that it is called....POP.WELL I HOPE THAT WILL SET EVERYBODY STRAGHT.||||reg||1
